fn main() { let s = S {}; println(s.d()); }` -> karac check: error[typecheck] 3:25 "ambiguous method 'm' on receiver of type 'S': multiple candidates apply" (`A.m(S)`, `B.m(S)`); expected 11. Cause: desugar::synthesize_trait_default_methods copies the default body into `impl A for S`, where the receiver is the concrete `S` and method lookup sees both traits' impls; written in the trait, `self` is `Self: A` and has one candidate (design.md §9 Generic receivers, and the ambiguity rule for `Self` in a trait body). Writing `A.m(self)` in the default works on check, interp and run (pinned in corpus/core/method_ufcs_names_the_trait). Found while pinning B-2026-11-04-8. Fix direction: check a copied default body with its trait preferred on an ambiguous method lookup of `self`, as a UFCS call naming the trait is; MIR lowering of the copy then needs the same trait (the two impls' `m` are named apart since B-2026-11-04-8).

