design.md §16 Resources each target provides: ProcessTable is native only; Effect-driven target gating: "A function reachable from an entry point that uses a resource the target lacks is error E0411, which shows the chain from the entry point to the resource use. It is an error whenever the build or check is for that target." The effect is inferred: `pub fn spawn_it()` calling `Command.new("true").status()` without a clause is refused with "performs effects [sends(ProcessTable), blocks, suspends]". Repro: `import std.process.{Command};
fn spawn_it() -> i64 { match Command.new("true").status() { Ok(_) => 1, Err(_) => 0 } }
fn helper() -> i64 { spawn_it() }
fn main() { println(helper()); }` -> `karac check x.kara --targets=all`: All checks passed under native, wasm_browser and wasm_wasi (only gpu fails, on Stdout); a package with `[build] targets = ["native", "wasm_wasi"]` or `["wasm_wasi"]`: All checks passed; `karac build --target=wasm_wasi x.kara` builds x.wasm, which under node's WASI prints 0 (status returned Err at run time). The gate itself exists (gpu refuses Stdout with a chain), so the wasm_wasi row of the provided-resource table seems to include ProcessTable. Cells: probe-core t16 w06_wasi_process_refused_E0411, k03, k07, k08.

