}`. `karac check`, `karac run`, `karac run --interp`, `karac build` and `karac run src/main.kara` (which finds the package) all abort with signal 6. Backtrace: Resolver::resolve_stmt <- resolve_block <- resolve_function <- resolve_items <- resolve <- cli::build_cmds::resolve_modules <- package_check_on <- run_check_cmds::package_check_refusal <- run_v2::package_source. So the package path resolves modules before the desugar pass that removes MultiAssign. The same file outside a package prints 2. A lib package (src/lib.kara with `pub fn sw(..) { ..; x, y = y, x; .. }`), a statement in a non-main module, and `v[0], v[1] = v[1], v[0]` all panic the same way. The tuple form `(p, q) = (..)` (refused with its E0287 fix) and struct spread `..s` do not panic. design.md §6 Parallel assignment calls this the in-place idiom swap sorts and permutation generators rely on. Found by probe:design-expressions package cells pk03/pk11.

